</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Statics of our evaluation datasets.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the scoring bias in LLM-as-a-Judge by perturbing the scoring prompt and observing whether the scoring judgments are affected, which follows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024c</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="Sx3.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Bias Types</h3>

<div id="Sx3.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define three types of bias targeting the key components related to scoring in LLM judges:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx3.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Sx3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score Rubrics Order</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Score IDs</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reference Answer Score</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx3.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Datasets</h3>

<div id="Sx3.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024c</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang, Lee, and Lukasik 2025</a>)</cite>, we select four LLM-as-a-Judge datasets for scoring bias evaluation:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx3.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="Sx3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BiGGen Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024b</a>)</cite>: This is a principled generation benchmark with instance-specific evaluation criteria. We use its test set for non-multilingual capabilities with 2,780 responses from 695 instances that are evaluated by human annotators.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FLASK</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. 2024b</a>)</cite>: This is a fine-grained evaluation benchmark with 200 test prompts, 12 score rubrics, and 2,001 responses. It also includes scores labeled by human annotators.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx3.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MT Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. 2023</a>)</cite>: This is a multi-turn chat benchmark with 80 test prompts. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024a</a>)</cite> write 80 hand-crafted score rubrics and generate 320 responses from WizardLM-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, Vicuna-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, Llama-2-Chat-13B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, and GPT-3.5-Turbo-0613 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI 2023a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx3.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx3.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx3.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx3.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vicuna Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al. 2023</a>)</cite>: This is a single-turn chat benchmark with 80 test prompts.<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2024a</a>)</cite> also write 80 hand-crafted score rubrics and generate 320 responses from WizardLM-13B, Vicuna-13B, Llama-2-Chat-13B, and GPT-3.5-Turbo-0613.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="Sx3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<table id="Sx3.T2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
